You are working on a React Native app written in TypeScript.

- Always use functional components and hooks; never class components.
- Do not use `any`. Prefer `unknown` and narrow it.
- Use the existing `api/` client for network calls; do not call fetch directly.
- Keep components under 200 lines; split them when they grow.
- Write tests with Jest and React Native Testing Library next to the component (`Foo.test.tsx`).
- Run `yarn tsc --noEmit` and `yarn test` before saying a task is done.
- Do not touch `ios/Pods` or `android/app/build`.
